        <headline>Wind Advisory issued September 24 at 6:00PM PDT until September 25 at 8:00PM PDT by NWS Portland OR</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Southwest winds 10 to 20 mph with gusts up to 50 mph
expected.

* WHERE...Upper Hood River Valley, particularly areas west of Oregon
Route 281.

* WHEN...From 8 AM to 8 PM PDT Friday.

* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree
limbs could be blown down and a few power outages may result.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Full leaf cover on trees may result in trees
or limbs suffering wind damage at lower wind speeds than usual.
</description>
        <instruction>Use extra caution when driving, especially if operating a high
profile vehicle. Secure outdoor objects such as garbage cans and
other objects that can easily blow around.</instruction>
